Usage: agent-deck feedback fixed N --fixed|--not-fixed [--comment C] [--dry-run] [--json] [--yes] [--from-agent] [--again]

Answer "Is it fixed for you?" on issue #N with a public comment:
  "Fixed for me in vX." or "Still broken for me in vX.", your comment (scrubbed:
  home paths become ~, tokens and host names are replaced), then (<os>/<arch>).
The CLI shows where it posts, as which GitHub account, and the exact text, then
asks y/N (default N). It posts with `gh issue comment` and records your answer
so What's new asks once; a second answer on the same report needs --again.

Flags:
  --fixed | --not-fixed   your answer (exactly one)
  --comment TEXT          optional comment
  --dry-run               print the exact comment; send nothing (--json adds account, gh_ready)
  --json                  JSON output, never prompts; posting also needs --yes
  --yes                   post without the y/N prompt
  --again                 answer a report you already answered
  --from-agent            an agent session answers: never prompts; only an unanswered report an
                          agent filed from this machine; needs [feedback] agent_reports (a person
                          runs 'agent-deck feedback agent-consent'; --yes does not stand in) and
                          AGENTDECK_INSTANCE_ID or --yes

Inside an agent session (AGENTDECK_INSTANCE_ID set), terminal or not, a post
is an agent's even without --from-agent: it refuses with consent_required unless
[feedback] agent_reports is on, and then takes the --from-agent path. --dry-run
sends nothing and runs the same checks (a refusal is ok:false with error_code).
